    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG Brady are delighted to bring this charming three-bedroom semi-detached property to the market, ideally located in the heart of the town centre.\nExtending to approximately 165 sq. m., this impressive listed building dates from the late 19th century and is described as a semi-detached rendered house featuring a distinctive gable and pierced bargeboard. Oozing charm, character and period appeal, the property offers a wonderful opportunity to acquire a substantial period residence in a highly convenient town-centre location.\nThe accommodation briefly comprises an entrance hall, living room, library, kitchen, conservatory, downstairs WC. and conservatory. Upstairs, there are three well-proportioned bedrooms, an additional WC and a separate shower room.\nThe property boasts a number of attractive period features, including beautiful coloured stained-glass windows, which add to the character and charm of this distinctive home. \nWhile the property would benefit from some care, attention and modernisation, it offers tremendous potential to create a stunning and unique residence while retaining its original period features.\nThe town-centre location provides exceptional convenience, with a wide range of shops, cafés, restaurants, schools, services and other local amenities all within easy reach. The combination of generous accommodation, period character and a central location makes this a particularly interesting property for those seeking a home with personality and potential.\nViewing is highly recommended to appreciate the generous accommodation, period character and excellent town-centre location this property has to offer."
      },
